# direnv / nix dev shell cache
.direnv/

# local logs / binaries
*.log
bin/
build/bin
# extracted ffmpeg binary distributions (e.g. ffmpeg-7.x-essentials_build/),
# NOT the backend/internal/ffmpeg source package
ffmpeg-*/

# vendored Windows ffmpeg/ffplay payload, copied into build/bin by the bundle task;
# large and separately licensed, so not committed
build/windows/redist/*.exe
# and the license text that arrives with it, which the release workflow downloads
build/windows/redist/ffmpeg-LICENSE.txt

# release artifacts: the tarball and zip the packaging scripts assemble
build/dist/

# What `task relay` draws for a relay on this machine: the certificate its TLS listeners hold,
# the key the group service signs tokens with, and the pair MediaMTX generates for its MoQ
# listener in whatever directory it runs from. Private keys among them, and every one of them is
# drawn again wherever it is absent.
/dev-relay/

# MediaMTX generates that MoQ pair beside itself, so a relay run by hand from the repository
# root leaves it here instead.
auto.crt
auto.key

# The pre-restructure module directory, which the "restructure" commit replaced and
# left behind untracked. What survives in it is the ffmpeg package as it stood then,
# kept only because two of its files were never committed anywhere.
#
# Anchored to the repository root: an unanchored "app/" matches a directory of that
# name at any depth, which silently swallowed the app package under internal/.
/_app/
